1
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:17,844
[Host] Welcome to Japanese Daily News. I'm Maya. Today is June eleventh. The rainy season has officially arrived across most of Japan — and on the traditional calendar, today is the very day it is said to begin. Let's listen.

2
00:00:18,443 --> 00:00:21,204
[News] 今日のニュースです。

3
00:00:21,903 --> 00:00:28,047
[News] 日本で、雨の多い「梅雨」の季節が始まりました。

4
00:00:28,748 --> 00:00:37,508
[News] 気象庁によると、関東甲信と東海は、今月7日ごろに梅雨入りしました。

5
00:00:38,207 --> 00:00:48,095
[News] 近畿や中国、九州など、ほかの多くの場所も、今月の初めに梅雨入りしています。

6
00:00:48,795 --> 00:00:57,076
[News] 梅雨は、6月から7月にかけて、雨や曇りの日が多くなる季節です。

7
00:00:57,776 --> 00:01:09,871
[News] 「梅雨」という言葉は、「梅」と「雨」の漢字で書きます。梅の実ができる時期の雨だから、と言われています。

8
00:01:10,572 --> 00:01:17,268
[News] 梅雨の間は、湿度が高くて、蒸し暑い日が続きます。

9
00:01:17,968 --> 00:01:24,927
[News] 毎日のように雨が降るので、洗濯物が乾きにくくなります。

10
00:01:25,628 --> 00:01:35,492
[News] 大雨が降ることもあるので、気象庁は、最新の天気予報に注意してほしいと話しています。

11
00:01:36,191 --> 00:01:41,256
[News] 梅雨が終わると、本格的な夏が来ます。

12
00:01:41,956 --> 00:01:49,132
[News] 雨の季節には、あじさいの花など、楽しみもたくさんあります。

13
00:01:49,831 --> 00:01:51,463
[Host] Let's break it down.

14
00:01:52,063 --> 00:01:59,096
[Slow] 日本で、雨の多い「梅雨」の季節が始まりました。

15
00:01:59,896 --> 00:02:05,536
[Host] In Japan, the rainy season — the rainiest weeks of the year — has begun.

16
00:02:06,135 --> 00:02:08,175
[Vocab] 梅雨

17
00:02:08,575 --> 00:02:16,183
[Host] It means the rainy season, the long stretch of wet weather in early summer. We'll hear where the name comes from in a moment.

18
00:02:16,783 --> 00:02:26,792
[Slow] 気象庁によると、関東甲信と東海は、今月7日ごろに梅雨入りしました。

19
00:02:27,592 --> 00:02:36,687
[Host] According to the Meteorological Agency, the regions around Tokyo and Nagoya entered the rainy season around the seventh of this month.

20
00:02:37,288 --> 00:02:39,639
[Vocab] 梅雨入り

21
00:02:40,039 --> 00:02:48,343
[Host] It means the start of the rainy season. The ending means entering — so the season is something you enter, like a door into weeks of rain.

22
00:02:48,943 --> 00:02:58,400
[Slow] 梅雨は、6月から7月にかけて、雨や曇りの日が多くなる季節です。

23
00:02:59,199 --> 00:03:05,991
[Host] The rainy season runs from June into July, a time when rainy and cloudy days become more common.

24
00:03:06,592 --> 00:03:08,824
[Vocab] 季節

25
00:03:09,223 --> 00:03:17,623
[Host] It means season. Japan is proud of having four distinct ones — this rainy stretch is sometimes called the unofficial fifth.

26
00:03:18,223 --> 00:03:32,048
[Slow] 「梅雨」という言葉は、「梅」と「雨」の漢字で書きます。梅の実ができる時期の雨だから、と言われています。

27
00:03:32,848 --> 00:03:40,599
[Host] The word is written with the characters for plum and rain — people say it's because the rain falls just when plums ripen.

28
00:03:41,199 --> 00:03:43,120
[Vocab] 梅

29
00:03:43,520 --> 00:03:51,848
[Host] It means plum. Plum blossoms open in early spring, and the fruit ripens right now — in the rain that carries its name.

30
00:03:52,448 --> 00:04:00,104
[Slow] 梅雨の間は、湿度が高くて、蒸し暑い日が続きます。

31
00:04:00,903 --> 00:04:06,903
[Host] During the rainy season, humidity stays high and hot, sticky days continue.

32
00:04:07,503 --> 00:04:10,096
[Vocab] 蒸し暑い

33
00:04:10,496 --> 00:04:18,079
[Host] It means hot and humid — that steamy, sticky kind of heat. The first part comes from the verb for steaming food.

34
00:04:18,680 --> 00:04:26,624
[Slow] 毎日のように雨が降るので、洗濯物が乾きにくくなります。

35
00:04:27,423 --> 00:04:32,295
[Host] Because it rains almost every day, laundry becomes hard to dry.

36
00:04:32,896 --> 00:04:35,632
[Vocab] 洗濯物

37
00:04:36,031 --> 00:04:42,367
[Host] It means laundry — the clothes you wash and hang up. A very real daily problem in this season.

38
00:04:42,968 --> 00:04:54,223
[Slow] 大雨が降ることもあるので、気象庁は、最新の天気予報に注意してほしいと話しています。

39
00:04:55,024 --> 00:05:02,944
[Host] Heavy rain sometimes falls, so the Meteorological Agency is asking people to keep an eye on the latest weather forecast.

40
00:05:03,543 --> 00:05:06,232
[Vocab] 天気予報

41
00:05:06,632 --> 00:05:12,800
[Host] It means weather forecast. The first half is weather, the second half means prediction.

42
00:05:13,399 --> 00:05:19,184
[Slow] 梅雨が終わると、本格的な夏が来ます。

43
00:05:19,983 --> 00:05:24,088
[Host] When the rainy season ends, full-blown summer arrives.

44
00:05:24,687 --> 00:05:27,447
[Vocab] 本格的

45
00:05:27,848 --> 00:05:37,232
[Host] It means full-scale, or the real thing. Real summer, real winter, even a restaurant's authentic curry — all described with this word.

46
00:05:37,831 --> 00:05:40,831
[Host] Let's listen to the full story one more time.

47
00:05:41,432 --> 00:05:44,192
[News] 今日のニュースです。

48
00:05:44,891 --> 00:05:51,036
[News] 日本で、雨の多い「梅雨」の季節が始まりました。

49
00:05:51,735 --> 00:06:00,495
[News] 気象庁によると、関東甲信と東海は、今月7日ごろに梅雨入りしました。

50
00:06:01,196 --> 00:06:11,084
[News] 近畿や中国、九州など、ほかの多くの場所も、今月の初めに梅雨入りしています。

51
00:06:11,783 --> 00:06:20,064
[News] 梅雨は、6月から7月にかけて、雨や曇りの日が多くなる季節です。

52
00:06:20,764 --> 00:06:32,860
[News] 「梅雨」という言葉は、「梅」と「雨」の漢字で書きます。梅の実ができる時期の雨だから、と言われています。

53
00:06:33,560 --> 00:06:40,255
[News] 梅雨の間は、湿度が高くて、蒸し暑い日が続きます。

54
00:06:40,956 --> 00:06:47,915
[News] 毎日のように雨が降るので、洗濯物が乾きにくくなります。

55
00:06:48,615 --> 00:06:58,480
[News] 大雨が降ることもあるので、気象庁は、最新の天気予報に注意してほしいと話しています。

56
00:06:59,180 --> 00:07:04,244
[News] 梅雨が終わると、本格的な夏が来ます。

57
00:07:04,944 --> 00:07:12,120
[News] 雨の季節には、あじさいの花など、楽しみもたくさんあります。

58
00:07:12,819 --> 00:07:15,555
[Host] Quiz time. Three questions.

59
00:07:16,156 --> 00:07:22,803
[Slow] 関東甲信と東海は、いつ梅雨入りしましたか。

60
00:07:23,603 --> 00:07:30,252
[Host] When did the regions around Tokyo and Nagoya enter the rainy season? Around the seventh of this month.

61
00:07:30,851 --> 00:07:37,908
[Slow] 「梅雨」という言葉には、どんな漢字が使われていますか。

62
00:07:38,708 --> 00:07:45,620
[Host] Which characters are used to write the name of this season? Plum and rain — because the rain falls when plums ripen.

63
00:07:46,220 --> 00:07:51,019
[Slow] 梅雨が終わると、何が来ますか。

64
00:07:51,819 --> 00:07:55,803
[Host] What comes when the rainy season ends? Full-blown summer.

65
00:07:56,403 --> 00:08:08,788
[Host] That's today's Japanese Daily News. Full transcript with furigana at podcast.jpnotes.dev. Subscribe on Apple Podcasts or Spotify. See you tomorrow.

66
